{"tool_name":"featurej-laplacian","contents":["neubias"],"fetched_metadata":{"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p>An often used Laplacian filter for enhancing signals at object boundaries and dots. It works with XY, XYZ, XYZ-T, XYZ-T-Ch1, XYZT-C1-C2 images. Distributed as a part of ImageJ plugin <a href=\"http://imagescience.org/meijering/software/featurej/\">FeatureJ</a>, and included in Fiji. The second URL above is the link to its Javadoc. (imagescience.feature.Laplacian). A primer for using this class in Jython script is in <a href=\"http://wiki.cmci.info/documents/120206pyip_cooking/python_imagej_cookbook\">CMCI Jython/Fiji cookbook: FeatureJ</a>.</p>","summary":"","value":"<p>An often used Laplacian filter for enhancing signals at object boundaries and dots. It works with XY, XYZ, XYZ-T, XYZ-T-Ch1, XYZT-C1-C2 images. Distributed as a part of ImageJ plugin <a href=\"http://imagescience.org/meijering/software/featurej/\">FeatureJ</a>, and included in Fiji. The second URL above is the link to its Javadoc. (imagescience.feature.Laplacian). A primer for using this class in Jython script is in <a href=\"http://wiki.cmci.info/documents/120206pyip_cooking/python_imagej_cookbook\">CMCI Jython/Fiji cookbook: FeatureJ</a>.</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2023-04-25T17:19:58+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2014-12-19T22:07:55+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[],"free_tagging":[],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":1505209964,"last_comment_uid":164,"status":2}],"has_author":[{"value":"Erik Meijering"}],"has_biological_terms":[],"has_comparison":[],"has_documentation":[],"has_doi":[],"has_entry_curator":[{"target_id":94,"target_type":"user","target_uuid":"aa749c9e-5b9a-4fdf-83ce-6b94538fe57c","url":"/user/94"}],"has_function":[{"target_id":4065,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","ta